---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { catalogue } from '../data/catalogue';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Strewnfields"
  description="Why Strewnfields is building a provenance-first public catalogue of meteorite locality and recovery evidence."
>
  <div class="page-shell">
    <header class="page-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">About the project</p>
      <h1>A catalogue that shows its work.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Strewnfields is an independent public project for comparing meteorite locality and
        recovery claims without stripping away their provenance, limits, or conflicts.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Why begin with {catalogue.length} records?</h2>
      <p>
        A small, varied catalogue exposes editorial edge cases before volume can hide them.
        These records test conflicting localities, different coordinate roles, and locations
        withheld from public mapping while keeping every assertion tied to evidence.
      </p>

      <h2>What this is not</h2>
      <p>
        It is not a hunting guide, land-status service, substitute for collection records,
        or promise that every source coordinate is accurate. It does not accept unsourced
        individual finds or create precise geometry from approximate prose.
      </p>

      <h2>Public now, durable later</h2>
      <p>
        The public sample is static and open to inspection. Its structured claims are
        designed to move into a spatial database without erasing source history. Any future
        private catalogue must use server-side authorization; protected coordinates will
        never be hidden inside public site assets or repository history.
      </p>

      <div class="card-grid">
        <article class="info-card">
          <h3>Transparent</h3><p>
            Every visible assertion retains a source locator and editorial state.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="info-card">
          <h3>Correctable</h3><p>
            Revision dates and durable claim IDs support review and change history.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="info-card">
          <h3>Restrained</h3><p>
            Missing geometry remains missing instead of being invented to fill a map.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <p><a class="button" href={`${base}explore/`}>Explore all public records</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
